  The host below is the production default. Builds resolve it from the same
  VITE_SITE_URL that canonical and og:url come from (vite.config.js), so a
  preview build cannot end up advertising production URLs, and the sitemap
  can never disagree with the canonicals.

  Deliberately absent: the error page and the form confirmation, which both
  carry a noindex tag; the extension-suffixed alternate of every page, each
  of which 301s to the clean URL above; and the 16 old WordPress paths that
  redirect here. No path appears literally in this comment, so a tool that
  greps the file rather than parsing it cannot mistake a note for an entry.

  No lastmod: a build date would claim all 25 pages changed at once, which
  is not true, and an invented date is worse than none. Real per-page dates
  can be taken from git history once these changes are committed.
-->
